Using the SAC Library
+++++++++++++++++++++

Overview
--------
In addition to being able to read and write SAC data files in one's own C or
FORTRAN programs (see `SAC Reading and Writing Routines`_ ), one can use many of
SAC's data-processing routines in stand-alone codes if one uses specific flags
in the compiling stage and the SAC libraries in the linking stage.  These
libraries libsac.a and libsacio.a are in ${SACHOME}/lib.  The complete
listing of sample programs in both C and Fortran are given below in the online
version of this file at <http://ds.iris.edu/files/sac-manual/manual/saclib.html>.

- Filtering_
- `Cut Data`_
- `Interpolate Data`_
- `Remove Mean`_
